# First run and project changes

This project uses **{{.training_layout}}**, **{{.engine}}** training and
**{{.inference_mode}}** inference. Run the commands below from this directory,
beside `databricks.yml`. Replace `YOUR_PROFILE` with your authenticated CLI profile.

## Where to make a change

The project has three configuration files: `config/features.yml` for optional
upstream feature groups, `config/training.yml` for models and training, and
`config/inference.yml` for scoring and model-set publication. Empty feature groups
add no job. Follow [FEATURE_TABLES.md](FEATURE_TABLES.md) to enable them.
Custom transformations and business functions remain ordinary Python.

| Change | Edit | Check afterwards |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Training source, record keys, shared limits and defaults | `config/training.yml` ? `defaults` | Preview names and selected columns; source tables must already exist. |
| Model, tuning, CV and quality policy | `config/training.yml` ? `models` | A model entry overrides shared defaults; nested mappings replace the whole value. |
| Scoring source, selection and change policy | `config/inference.yml` | Review the saved version and output destination. |
{{if eq .training_layout "multi_target"}}| Whole-set release policy and output tables/views | `config/inference.yml` ? `model_set` | Review the complete set before activation. |
{{end}}| Fixed eligibility rules before splitting | `src/features/pre_split.py` | Preserve the record-key contract and document excluded rows. |
| Learned preprocessing | `src/features/preprocessing.py` | Fit statistics inside each training fold; scoring uses the saved fitted recipe. |
| Shared Spark feature tables | `src/features/groups/`, `config/features.yml` | Compute shared features, refresh the feature graph, and run it before downstream training/scoring. |
| Business output rules | `src/features/scoring.py` | Check typed output columns and required components before retraining. |
| Workspace, schemas, Run-as identities and job permissions | `deployment/targets.yml`, `deployment/variables.yml` | Review the selected target and downstream job permissions. |
| Core wheel/source and required release | `deployment/artifact.json` | Build the wheel and inspect `dist/skyulf/build.json`. |
| Runtime dependencies | `deployment/requirements.txt`, `src/features/requirements.txt` | Install and verify matching versions before deployment. |
| Monitoring tables, labels and retraining policies | Target variables in `deployment/targets.yml` | Start with performance `mode: report`; inspect saved evidence before enabling retraining. |
| Job task graph | `resources/*.job.yml` | Validate the Bundle after regenerating the training graph when declarations change. |

The thin notebooks in `src/jobs/` call Skyulf's library. Ordinary model and recipe
changes belong in the files above. Regenerating a project is not an in-place
upgrade: preserve your edited declarations and apply template changes deliberately.

## 1. Check the project locally

Install the matching Skyulf Core wheel and the project's declared dependencies in
your local Python environment. Configure `deployment/artifact.json` with the source
checkout or wheel you intend to deploy; keep that source outside `dist/skyulf/`.

```powershell
python src/tools/smoke.py
python src/tools/preview.py --action train
uv run --no-project python src/tools/build_wheel.py
```

`smoke.py` validates configuration and source syntax without running editable
Python hooks. When present, `src/features/` and `src/composition/` also go through
training's package snapshot checks: package boundaries, declared asset files,
exact dependency pins and saved-source size limits. Dependencies are not imported
or installed. A failure exits with code 1 and prints JSON identifying the file or
package and reason; syntax errors also include the file, line and column.
Successful output lists the checked packages in `project_packages`.
It does not prove data access, model fit, or deployment permissions.
`preview.py` executes your trusted recipe builders, but does not read training
tables or train. Keep I/O out of imports and builders. Both tools accept explicit
catalog/schema/suffix bindings; they do not resolve `deployment/targets.yml` for
you. Use the values of the target you will deploy.

Review `dist/skyulf/build.json`: release, filename and SHA-256 identify the wheel
bytes that will be uploaded. The builder rejects a mismatched release.

## 2. Validate and deploy the selected target

Fill the selected target's workspace, catalog/schema and identity values before
running these commands. `REPLACE_*` values are deployment inputs to complete.
Catalog/schema privileges and job-to-job execution rights are separate; see
[deployment setup](deployment/README.md).

```powershell
databricks bundle validate --strict -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE
databricks bundle deploy -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE
```

Deploy creates `train`, `score` and `monitoring` jobs. It does not train a model or
create the input data. Monitoring uses its own serverless environment, including
when training/scoring use a policy cluster. Personal targets start isolated with
paused schedules; review shared-target schedules before deploying.

## 3. Train, inspect the decision, then score

```powershell
databricks bundle run -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE train
```

{{if eq .training_layout "model_competition"}}Each candidate trains on the shared training folds. `select_best_model` ranks
training-side CV results; only its winner receives the reserved holdout and
champion checks. Open `training_report` for the result and exact operator action.
A failed winner does not automatically promote the runner-up.
{{else if eq .training_layout "multi_target"}}Open each `train_<name>` result, then the `training_report` task (its notebook is
`models_report.py`) and the set's `model_decision` task.
The complete set has one pinned release; approve it as a set after all required
component checks pass. `training.yml` controls fitting; `inference.yml` controls
activation and publication.
{{else}}Open `train_and_tune` for search/fitting evidence and `training_report` for the
final decision. A registered candidate is not necessarily the active champion.
{{end}}

A manual policy leaves a passing candidate pending approval. Use the exact
approve/reject/rollback parameters shown by the report; these refer to saved
evidence. Confirm the selected concrete model or set version before scoring.
When `score_handoff=after_alias_change` has already started a child score run,
inspect that run before starting another one.

```powershell
databricks bundle run -t {{if eq .personal_development_targets "true"}}test_development{{else}}test{{end}} --profile YOUR_PROFILE score
```

Open `scoring_report` for the committed result and source/selection provenance.
Enable Delta Change Data Feed on the scoring source before new rows arrive.
The initial scoring run processes existing source rows. Later behavior follows
the configured source-change and model-change policies.

## 4. Inspect monitoring

A successful score commit can hand off to the separate `monitoring` job when
monitoring is enabled. Its schedule can also check delayed labels. Open
`monitoring_report` for drift, observed performance and performance-loss evidence;
open `evaluate_retraining` for the saved policy decision and request, if eligible.
Drift or performance loss can request retraining, subject to the configured
freshness, row/label coverage, cooldown and request guards. Retraining still uses
the normal training, quality and promotion rules.

The shared native dashboard reads saved monitoring tables. Its refresh task
updates the dashboard cache; it does not calculate new observations. See the
[monitoring guide](src/monitoring/README.md) for table setup, labels, policies,
refresh and online-serving diagnostics.

## Find the failing stage

| Symptom | First evidence to inspect | Next action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Local smoke or preview fails | Printed field/recipe error | Fix the named setting or builder; preview does not test table permissions. |
| Wheel build rejects the version | `deployment/artifact.json` and wheel metadata | Point at the intended release; keep source and generated output separate. |
| Bundle validation fails | Target overrides and unresolved placeholders | Check the working directory, profile, target, YAML and resource references. |
| Training stops before fitting | First failed task and original traceback | Check the source snapshot, keys, labels, input bounds and schema. |
| Search runs longer than expected | Candidate/branch tuning settings and progress | Count trials, folds, nested searches and final refits; tune the budget explicitly. |
| Candidate is registered but scoring cannot use it | Final promotion decision and score selection | Complete the required approval or correct the pinned selection. |
| A parent succeeds but a downstream job cannot start | Calling task and target job ACL | Grant the configured Run-as principal the documented downstream execution right. |
| Dashboard is empty or stale | Enrollment, latest saved observation, monitor run, then refresh run | Confirm the monitoring identity and table namespace before changing chart filters. |
| Performance is unavailable | Label join, availability time and coverage reason | Supply matching outcomes and wait for the eligible window; missing labels are not healthy performance. |

Record the failing job/run/task, target, model/set version and first traceback.
The final report points to durable evidence; a report task's success alone does
not prove that fitting, promotion or scoring succeeded. For detailed contracts,
continue with the [project reference](README.md).
